findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. The
    reviewer flagged silent unknown fields but not the broader error-swallowing in
    from_file_or_default.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: "Dev implemented sanitized Display impl for CliError. Reviewer verified:\
    \ 'CWE-209 error display \u2014 CliError::Display impl sanitizes output, does\
    \ not expose inner ServerError messages. Tests verify this.' However, the reviewer\
    \ did not flag that eprintln still prints Display directly to stderr without a\
    \ user_message() method, so the mitigation is partial."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA wrote header injection tests for CRLF/null bytes, and Dev implemented
    validate_header_value rejecting those characters. However, tenant_id is still
    a raw String rather than using axiathon-core's validated TenantId type. The type-safety
    gap was not flagged by any phase.
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as [MEDIUM]: 'Neither version is in [workspace.dependencies]\
    \ in the root Cargo.toml despite the story spec saying to add it there. Same for\
    \ reqwest, comfy-table, keyring, clap_complete, dirs, and csv \u2014 none are\
    \ workspace-managed. This creates version drift risk across crates.'"
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as [HIGH]: 'RawConfig uses #[derive(Deserialize, Default)]\
    \ without #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)]. An operator who typos server_url as serverurl\
    \ or server-url gets no error \u2014 the field is silently ignored and defaults\
    \ are used.'"
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as [MEDIUM]: 'config_rejects_server_url_without_scheme\
    \ test is vacuous \u2014 tests/security.rs:109-124. This test allows either an\
    \ Err return or an Ok with a valid scheme. It never asserts the specific behavior.'\
    \ Also flagged the config_file_permissions test as similarly vacuous."
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the specific test that uses 'let _ = config;' with zero
    assertions. The reviewer caught other vacuous test patterns but not this specific
    zero-assertion test.
